\section*{Cost Volume Summary}

This Volume 3 Cost Volume presents the basis of estimate (BOE) and detailed cost breakdown for the Atelier Logic Group LLC Phase I effort under Army SBIR Topic ARM26TX04-NV001. The proposed price is \textbf{\$200,000.00}, including fixed fee of \textbf{\$13,084.11} (7.00\% on total estimated cost). All labor hours are aligned with the 6-month technical work plan described in Volume 2.

\section{Direct Labor Breakdown}

\begin{table}[H]
\centering
\small
\caption{Phase I Direct Labor Breakdown}
\label{tab:direct-labor}
\begin{tabular}{@{}lrrr@{}}
\toprule
\textbf{Role} & \textbf{Hours} & \textbf{Rate (USD)} & \textbf{Amount (USD)} \\
\midrule
Principal Investigator (Ishmael Ibrahim Amin) & 480 & 95.00 & 45,600.00 \\
Senior Embedded Engineer & 360 & 85.00 & 30,600.00 \\
\midrule
\textbf{Subtotal Direct Labor} & \textbf{840} & --- & \textbf{76,200.00} \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

\smallskip
The 840 direct labor hours correspond to the six-month Phase I schedule (Tasks 1--4): requirements and architecture, kernel design and fixed-point ABI, host and ARM HIL validation, and equivalence testing with final reporting. The PI provides systems architecture and SBIR direction; the Senior Embedded Engineer implements the Rust kernel, C ABI, and bare-metal target integration.

